To enable support in FlightGear you must manually copy some of the files
from this directory tree to proper FlightGear directories. See ltr_pipe's
README file for usage information.

* Files description
====================

Stand-alone protocol file:

  fgfs/Protocol/linuxtrack.xml


Protocol file for linuxtrack.nas script:

  fgfs/Protocol/linuxtrack.nas.xml


Nasal script for linuxtrack.nas.xml protocol file:

  fgfs/Nasal/LinuxTrack/linuxtrack.nas


Example joystick file:

  fgfs/Input/Joysticks/LinuxTrack/uinput-abs.xml


* FGCamera Integration
=======================

This plugin automatically detects when the FGCamera addon is active and has
its LinuxTrack handler enabled. When detected, this plugin will:

  - Continue to provide protocol setup (data feed to /sim/linuxtrack/data/*)
  - Defer view control to FGCamera's offset management system
  - Automatically resume direct view control if FGCamera is disabled

This ensures both plugins can work together without conflicts. The protocol
data feed remains active regardless of FGCamera status, allowing FGCamera to
consume the tracking data through its handler system.

To force direct view control even when FGCamera is active, set:

  --prop:/sim/linuxtrack/force-direct-control=1

Note: This property defaults to 0 (automatic detection enabled).

